            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kate"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad is fantastic AS IS. No alterations. OK, maybe some slight alterations with amounts b/c I rarely use exact amounts on anything. I just kind of eyeball it and go yup, that looks good. Oh, and I used Brianna's creamy poppyseed dressing. Absolutely perfect! I get rave reviews wherever I serve it."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Michele Southwick"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used baby arugula instead of cabbage, craisins instead of raisins, and slivered almonds for the nuts. My family loves it!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-28T00:28:21.743Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ljones35"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great salad I made a few alterations though, I omited the golden raisens and the onion. The whole bottle of dressing is crazy I only use a couple splashes I add more strawberries and grapes than what is recommended and it comes out fantastic!!! My favorite summer salad! Great party salad!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-14T12:00:46.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Grayhaired mama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was pretty good, but there were quite a few flavors going on with it, and it made soooo much. It doesn't need the whole bottle of dressing at all. We just tossed it around until it was all lightly coated. \r\nI added more grapes, due to other reviews, but I think if I make it again, I will keep as is. I didn't use pine nuts either...almonds were just fine. Also, there were too many raisins for my tastes, and too much red onion...it was rather overpowering, so we picked some of it out.",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-03T15:00:34.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cookingmama2103"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had this salad at a wedding once. And I went in search for the recipe and found it here. So GOOD! The only thing that I changed was I didn't use pine nuts. Instead I used walnuts. I couldn't find pine nuts at the store. And I had walnuts in my cupboard. Turned out great. I also didn't use a whole bottle of dressing. Maybe 1/4 of the bottle. What a great summer salad.",
            "datePublished": "2012-10-08T07:04:34.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
